# PRE20-ALIGN DB Drift Table

## Missing `org_id` Tables

| Table | Classification | Severity | Alignment Finding | Required Productization Decision |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| callback_state_transitions | Execution history | High | Durable transition rows are not directly tenant-scoped | Add tenant shape or guarantee all access joins through callback_state org scope |
| user_permission_assignments | Permission grant state | High | Uses scope_type/scope_key, not org_id | Decide whether org grants need DB-native org_id and C18G coverage |
| shared_modules | Cross-org business relation | Medium | Uses source_org_id/target_org_id, not org_id | Keep explicit dual-org access rules; do not rely on C18G automatic filtering |
| users | Global identity | Medium | Global identity table | Product UI must avoid treating all users as tenant-local |
| auth_sessions | Global session state | Medium | Global session table | Do not use as tenant boundary; rely on org context/membership |
| security_rate_limit_buckets | Security operational state | Medium | Global keyed bucket table | Ensure keys encode tenant where tenant rate limits are required |
| security_replay_nonces | Security operational state | Medium | Global replay nonce table | Ensure keys encode tenant where tenant replay isolation is required |
| agent_registry | Global registry | Low | No org_id by design | Safe only as global metadata catalog |
| module_registry | Global registry | Low | No org_id by design | Tenant activation must remain in module_bindings |
| workflow_registry | Global registry | Low | No org_id by design | Safe only as global template catalog |
| permission_registry | Global permission catalog | Low | No org_id by design | Safe as catalog; grants are separate |
| role_default_permissions | Global role defaults | Low | No org_id by design | Safe as global defaults |

Excluded by scope: C19 `messages` lacks `org_id`, and C19 `contact_identities` has `org_id`; both are intentionally excluded from PRE20-ALIGN scoring.

