## Memory-Only Or Non-DB-Managed State

| Component | State | Risk |
|---|---|---|
| C08 module adapter registry | Static in-code contracts | Adapter catalog cannot be product-managed as data |
| C09 provider registry | Static in-code contracts | Provider availability cannot be product-managed as data |
| C10 sandbox runtime | Request-bound mock memory/log/state refs | No durable real runtime execution state |
| Event collector worker | In-memory queue counters and drain worker | Operational queue state not durable, though source events are persisted |
| LiveGatingController fallback | In-memory policy map path exists | Non-DB path can diverge from persisted policies |
| InMemoryStorageAdapter | Memory storage implementation | Must remain test/design-only |
| Execution request/plan | No first-class table found | Execution decisions are not product-traceable as durable records |

## Schema Drift From C05 Baseline

| Area | C05/F07 Baseline | PRE20 Current State | Drift |
|---|---|---|---|
| Permission assignments | C05 assignment table without org_id | Still no org_id; uses scope_type/scope_key | Unresolved tenant-shape drift |
| Owner access semantics | C05 text expected owner global full access | Current service reports owner as platform owner, not full access; unified engine restricts owner categories | Semantic drift |
| Core records | F07 jobs/artifacts/reviews/errors/memory/operation tables initially global | C18 added org_id to core business records | Resolved |
| Approvals | Approval persistence existed outside C05 baseline | C18 added org_id; approval_decisions scoped | Aligned |
| C15 durable state | Not in C05 | Added callbacks/results/DLQ/callback_state/dlq_state; transition table unscoped | Partial drift |
| C17 observability | Not in C05 | Added event/audit/replay/anomaly/storage tables with org_id | Mostly aligned |
| PRE20 ops/live gate | Not in C05 | Added live gate, canary, rollback, alert, unlock tables with org_id | Aligned |
| Registries | Global catalogs | Remain global | Acceptable if catalog-only |

